<title>CANADA: Prairies avoid frost Wed night, SW Alberta at risk.</title>
<headline>Prairies avoid frost Wed night, SW Alberta at risk.</headline>
<dateline>WINNIPEG 1996-09-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Canada's Prairie grainbelt avoided frost Wednesday night but southwest Alberta was at risk of a light frost Thursday night, Environment Canada said.</p>
<p>Edson, Alberta, west of Edmonton reported an overnight low of 1.0 Celsius (33.8 F) at chest level, meteorologist Gerald Machnee told Reuters.</p>
<p>&quot;But Edson was cloudy with rain all night so they probably didn't get a frost,&quot; Machnee said.</p>
<p>Southwest Alberta was forecast to see an overnight low Thursday night of 2.0 Celsius (35.6 F) under clearer skies placing the region at a slight risk of frost, he said.</p>
<p>-- Gilbert Le Gras 204 947 3548</p>
